--TEST--
A written `Core\Config::set` or `restore` name that no request may change does not compile, and a template no settable key fits warns — `rule:config/three-changeability-classes`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: tools:config/reading-and-changing-it-from-a-program-core-config
// `server.listen` is set only in `nvs.toml`, and `my.own.setting` is no setting at all.
// Both calls would change nothing on every server, so both names are compile errors.
Core\Config::set('server.listen', '0.0.0.0:9000');
Core\Config::restore('my.own.setting');

// No setting a program may change has the form `db.<something>.driver`, so this warns.
string $name = 'main';
Core\Config::set("db.{$name}.driver", 'sqlite');

// A listed key compiles, in the same file, so the name is what is refused.
Core\Config::set('memory', '64M');
Core\Config::restore('memory');
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0667]: a program cannot change the setting `server.listen`
%A
error[E0667]: a program cannot change the setting `my.own.setting`
%A
warning[W1037]: no setting a program may change has a name of this form, so `set` changes nothing
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors; 1 warning emitted
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
